{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:bd8900273cedc374","name":"Fragmentation Wire","source":{"id":"source:reference-bd8900273cedc374","title":"Fragmentation Wire","revision":26656,"timestamp":"2025-04-18T21:49:11Z","sha256":"8efb193e5f7c7d393b6f7275ef2992503603d18ec62151b55099fe9b6226d4a6","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=26656","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Fragmentation%20Wire&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-bd8900273cedc374","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Galaxy at War"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Galaxy_at_War"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Cost:"]}," 100/Meter\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Weight:"]}," 2 Kilograms/Meter\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Availability:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Military"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Military"},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Fragmentation Wire is a particularly nasty form of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Razor Wire"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Razor_Wire","referenceId":"reference:123c9d86b35b66e6"}," that explodes when it is tampered with, spraying hundreds of tiny fragments through its area. Fragmentation Wire is often interspersed with normal ",{"tag":"a","children":["Razor Wire"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Razor_Wire","referenceId":"reference:123c9d86b35b66e6"},". The two are similar, but an observer can tell the difference with a successful DC 20 ",{"tag":"a","children":["Perception"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Perception","referenceId":"reference:bd18e320a6bb9f53"}," check.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Squares featuring Fragmentation Wire are considered ",{"tag":"a","children":["Difficult Terrain"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Difficult_Terrain"},". If a character enters a square containing Fragmentation Wire, the wire makes a +10 attack, which is compared to the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Reflex Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Reflex_Defense"}," of the target. If successful, the Fragmentation Wire detonates, dealing 2d6 damage in a 1-square ",{"tag":"a","children":["Splash"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Splash"}," and destroying the Fragmentation Wire in that square. Fragmentation Wire that has been destroyed cannot ",{"tag":"a","children":["Immobilize"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Immobilize"}," a target.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Each square of Fragmentation Wire has ",{"tag":"a","children":["Damage Reduction"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Damage_Reduction"}," 1, 4 ",{"tag":"a","children":["Hit Points"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Hit_Points","referenceId":"reference:58e8ee2c9538d027"},", a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Damage Threshold"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Damage_Threshold"}," of 10, and a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Break DC"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Break_DC"}," of 15. Breaking Fragmentation Wire results in detonation of the wire.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Damage:"]}," 2d6 (Slashing)\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Radius:"]}," 1-Square (",{"tag":"a","children":["Splash"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Splash"},")\n"]},"\n","\n","\n","\n\n","\n\n","\n"]}}
